          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"dumas-fils-la-dame-aux-camelias-697fbf6647d5\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.94,\"analysis\":\"The speaker directly avows the magnitude of a present loving state: “you do not know how much I love you.” The utterance contains no explicit relational undertaking or commitment. Its exclamation mark and emphatic scalar construction indicate intensity but do not independently establish expressive/reflexive force.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The narrow extract does not identify the interlocutors or immediate motive, so reassurance, protest, or persuasion may be contextually involved; none changes the dominant truth-conditional force established by the wording.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"A directly presented line of dialogue in which the speaker tells the addressee how strongly the speaker loves them.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"“C’est que tu ne sais pas combien…” frames the avowal as an explanation or corrective: the addressee allegedly fails to appreciate the depth of the speaker’s love. This gives the declaration emphatic and potentially persuasive force, but the supplied passage provides no evidence of a commitment-enacting act or of reflex-like verbal discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"local-1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“C'est que tu ne sais pas combien je t'aime!”\",\"supports\":\"The first-person present-tense clause explicitly presents the speaker’s love, and its degree, as true, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"local-2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The degree construction “combien” and the exclamation mark intensify the avowal.\",\"supports\":\"These features support emphatic emotional delivery, but without additional evidence they do not establish independent E force or a P-type undertaking.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"metadata-1\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is located in Chapter XVIII of Alexandre Dumas fils’s La Dame aux camélias and is presented with a dialogue dash.\",\"supports\":\"This supports treating the occurrence as direct fictional dialogue rather than narration, report, or writing.\",\"confidence\":0.98}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core avowal. Emotional emphasis can be recorded contextually without adding E, while no undertaking supports P and no residual core force requires O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
